**How to implement.** The study view's Results step: the chosen fit run's results in six tabs (001 §O 'results tabs: values, correlation, residuals, realizability, product check, profile likelihood'; 001 §L 'Results, stored in the fit run: value ± σ …; correlation matrix, rank, condition; per-experiment residuals and RMSE; Mueller realizability …; the product check …; post-fit identifiability by profile likelihood'). It shows what the fit run stores (`FitRun.results`, steps 396, 404) and computes nothing. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `ConstructorFlowStep` gains `ResultsFlowStep` after `FitFlowStep`, its `caption` `Results` and its `flowUiId` `flowResultsStep`, one of the study's steps (step 414). Before `StudySurfaceState`: `FitResultsTab` = `ValuesResultsTab` | `CorrelationResultsTab` | `ResidualsResultsTab` | `RealizabilityResultsTab` | `ProductCheckResultsTab` | `ProfileResultsTab`, in 001 §O's order, with `static member all`, `member this.caption : ControlCaption` (`Values`, `Correlation`, `Residuals`, `Realizability`, `Product check`, `Profile likelihood`) and `member this.tabUiId : ConstructorUiId` (its box's id, below); window state, never stored, so no tag. `StudySurfaceState` gains `resultsTab : FitResultsTab`, `ValuesResultsTab` initially; `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `ShowResultsTab of FitResultsTab`, which sets it and writes nothing. On the model extension holding `studyPrefitsOpt` (step 415), each documented in one line: `member model.selectedFitRunOpt : FitRun option`, the run of `model.studyFitRuns` that `fitRunOpt` names, else the latest of them, else `None`; `member model.ownerCaption (owner : UnknownOwner) : ControlCaption`, the item's label, `<the material's name> v<n>`, `session <name>` or `run <name>` (step 362); and `member model.fitEntryCaption (entry : FitEntryRef) : ControlCaption`, `<its owner's caption> <the parameter's name>` (step 396). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, a group after the Fit step's under `// --- The study's Results step (StudyResultsView). ---`, each with a one-line doc: `flowResultsStep` (`"FlowResultsStep"`), `studyResultsPanel` (`"StudyResultsPanel"`), `fitResultsRunText` (`"FitResultsRunText"`), `fitResultsTabStrip` (`"FitResultsTabStrip"`), `fitResultsValuesTab` (`"FitResultsValuesTab"`), `fitResultsCorrelationTab` (`"FitResultsCorrelationTab"`), `fitResultsResidualsTab` (`"FitResultsResidualsTab"`), `fitResultsRealizabilityTab` (`"FitResultsRealizabilityTab"`), `fitResultsProductCheckTab` (`"FitResultsProductCheckTab"`), `fitResultsProfileTab` (`"FitResultsProfileTab"`) and `fitResultsTable` (`"FitResultsTable"`, the shown tab's table). (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyResultsView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyResultsView`, compiled directly after `StudyFitView.fs` (step 415): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `studyResultsView (model) (dispatch) : IView`, its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5: a `ScrollViewer` scrolling both ways around a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `studyResultsPanel`, margin 8, holding `StudyUnknownsView.studyBarView` and, for `model.selectedFitRunOpt`: `Fit run <name> — <stage.text>, <engine.text>` (`fitResultsRunText`); a `WrapPanel` carrying `fitResultsTabStrip` of one box per `FitResultsTab.all` carrying its `tabUiId` with its `caption`, sending `ShowResultsTab`, the chosen one on `positiveBackground`; and the chosen tab's table carrying `fitResultsTable`, every number `ToString("G6", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)` as the parameter grid writes them (step 241). Values: a `Grid` of `Parameter`, `Start`, `Fitted` and `σ`, one row per `run.entries` entry (step 383) by `model.fitEntryCaption`, its σ that of `results.sigmas` or `undetermined`. Correlation: per `results.problems` element, the line `<subject>: rank <r>, condition <c or —>, χ² <x>, RMSE <rmse>` (`StudyEntriesProblem` written `Study residual`, `ObjectSolveProblem items` `Object <the items' labels>`, `AirFringeProblem runs` `AIR fringe <the runs>`), then, with a correlation matrix, a `Grid` whose header row and column are its coordinates (an `EntryCoordinate`'s entries' captions joined by `, `, `ElementCoordinate (r, c)` written `m<r><c>`, `FringeVisibilityCoordinate` written `fringe visibility`) and whose cells are ρ written `F3`, and without one the line `no correlation: the Jacobian is rank-deficient`. Residuals: per `results.runResiduals`, `<run>: RMSE <rmse> over <n> residual(s)`. Realizability: per `results.realizability`, `<the item's label>: realizable` or `not realizable` (`ObjectRealizability.realizability`, step 396), `; eigenvalues <the four>`. Product check: per `results.productChecks`, `<the items' labels joined by → >: product RMSE <p>, fit RMSE <f>, ratio <rmseRatio>, max |ΔM| <difference.maxAbs>` (steps 352, 400). Profile likelihood: per `results.profiles`, `<the entry's caption> (<its reasons>)`, each reason `σ undetermined`, `σ is <fraction> of its bounds` or `correlated with <the partner's caption> (ρ = <ρ>)`, then one line per point, `<value>: χ² <x>` or `<value>: <the failure's text>`. A tab with nothing reads `Nothing to show for this fit run.`; without a fit run the panel ends with `No fit run yet: run the fit in the Fit step.`. (4) `KitWindowView.fs`: `ResultsFlowStep` shows `StudyResultsView.studyResultsView model dispatch` keyed `results`. Tests. `StudyWindowModelTests` gains `a results tab and a fit run choose what the Results step shows, the study's latest run by default`: with two fit runs of `QZ-LR` loaded and `fitRunOpt` `None`, `selectedFitRunOpt` is the later; after `SelectFitRun` of the earlier it is the earlier; `ShowResultsTab CorrelationResultsTab` sets the surface's tab; `FitResultsTab.all` is the six in 001 §O's order with their captions. `StudyViewTests`: `the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins the Results step's ids and each tab's `tabUiId`; without a trait, `the Results step shows the chosen fit run's six tabs and each tab's table`: over `studyKitIn` with a test-local fit run of `QZ-LR` written through `writeFitRun` whose results hold one value of each list (its correlation matrix 2 × 2 and its profile of seven points), as step 404's round-trip run holds them, on `ResultsFlowStep` with each tab chosen in turn through `ShowResultsTab`, `fitResultsTable` holds CPL1's `c2.retardance` with its σ, the study residual's rank and a 2 × 2 correlation grid, the run's RMSE, the realizable object's eigenvalues, the series' ratio and the profile's seven points; with trait `ui-smoke`, `pressing each results tab shows its table`: pressing each `tabUiId` in turn shows that tab's `fitResultsTable`. `KitWindowTests`: `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `FlowResultsStep`; `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` also finds the Results box below Fit and, on `ResultsFlowStep`, `studyResultsPanel`. `KitWindowModelTests`: `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups` adds Results; `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it` also finds `stepsOf ForwardConstructor` without Results. `ScrollExtentTests` gains `the kit window's Results step leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable "KitWindowResults"` over `kitWindowView` on `ResultsFlowStep` with the correlation tab of a run whose problem holds a 16 × 16 correlation matrix.

**Acceptance.** After the Results step lands, the Inverse constructor's flow strip MUST show Results after Fit, and `studyResultsView` MUST show the chosen fit run, the study's latest by default, in six tabs (values, correlation, residuals, realizability, product check, profile likelihood) of what its results store; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a results tab and a fit run choose what the Results step shows, the study's latest run by default`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups` and `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it`; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing each results tab shows its table`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Results step shows the chosen fit run's six tabs and each tab's table` and `the kit window's Results step leaves everything reachable`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` and `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows`; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.
